From 7192f9ea35b7e839ee12948cdb7fc908ccdd9929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:30:28 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] 034 A2 r2 (TKOffset): extra shells of a thick solid are legal
 cavities, a detached wall is an error

Review of A2 r1: the shell-count bound (1 per open piece of the kept faces,
2 per closed piece) rejected EXACT thick solids whose offset pinches off
at a neck thinner than 2|t| (or seals a slot narrower than 2t outward):
the unreachable part of the hollow is a closed cavity, one more shell.

Every face of the glued thick solid is now classified by its generator,
read from the offset history (myInitOffsetFace) and the gluing copies:
kept input face, wall (image of a removed face), offset (image of a kept
face, edge or vertex). A shell is ANCHORED (holds kept faces) or not.
The wall of an opening is the band of the removed face between its rim
and the offset, so every piece of it touches the rim (Rossignac-Requicha
1986 shelling; own derivation):
- a shell without kept faces that holds a wall is impossible (the offset
  shell was closed across the opening): error, always, O(F+E);
- more shells than the pieces give are accepted when every shell without
  kept faces is made of known offset faces only and every wall meets an
  offset face (cavities of the hollow); otherwise the extra shell is not
  explained and the result is checked (BRepCheck + BOP self-interference,
  the review's safety net), error only if that fails.
The count bound stays only as the gate of the second rule. Closed and
coherent shells (check 1) and the tangent free-form check (3) unchanged.
NCollection_Vector -> NCollection_DynamicArray (deprecated alias).

Exports unchanged (480 = weekly); imports + BRepTools_Quilt::Copy and
::IsCopied (exported by the weekly TKBRep).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
